1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,788
Two traders. The same system, the same trades.

2
00:00:09,238 --> 00:00:14,959
The system has an edge. Yet by year end, one account was cut in half.

3
00:00:15,408 --> 00:00:19,771
Only one thing was different: how much each one risked per trade.

4
00:00:20,771 --> 00:00:25,604
Hello, this is episode six of the SPIDER Quant Trading series.

5
00:00:26,054 --> 00:00:31,930
Last time: backtesting, how to test a system before risking money.

6
00:00:32,381 --> 00:00:37,371
Today: risk of ruin, the chance of blowing the account.

7
00:00:38,371 --> 00:00:42,158
Ruin does not have to mean the account hits zero.

8
00:00:42,608 --> 00:00:47,598
Ruin is the level from which coming back becomes almost impossible.

9
00:00:48,048 --> 00:00:54,317
Remember episode three: after a 50% fall, you need 100% just to get back.

10
00:00:54,767 --> 00:00:59,678
So today we will call it ruin when the account is cut in half.

11
00:01:00,678 --> 00:01:03,447
The chance of ruin depends on three things.

12
00:01:03,897 --> 00:01:10,244
One, the win rate. Two, the size of wins versus losses, the R.

13
00:01:10,695 --> 00:01:14,979
And three, what percent of the account you risk per trade.

14
00:01:15,428 --> 00:01:21,306
The system decides the first two. The third is entirely in your hands.

15
00:01:22,306 --> 00:01:24,735
How common is a long losing streak?

16
00:01:25,186 --> 00:01:29,235
Take a system that wins 50% of the time, over 500 trades.

17
00:01:29,684 --> 00:01:35,014
The chance of eight losses in a row somewhere is about 62%.

18
00:01:35,464 --> 00:01:41,262
Even ten in a row has about a 21% chance. This is very common.

19
00:01:42,262 --> 00:01:46,547
Now see where the account is after ten straight losses.

20
00:01:46,997 --> 00:01:53,919
At 1% risk, about 10% down. At 2%, about 18%.

21
00:01:54,369 --> 00:02:00,979
At 5%, 40% down. And at 10% risk, 65% down.

22
00:02:01,428 --> 00:02:06,026
So big risk, one bad week, and the game is over.

23
00:02:07,026 --> 00:02:13,948
Now a simulation. The system wins 50% of the time, and each win is 1.5 times a loss.

24
00:02:14,399 --> 00:02:20,275
That is a positive edge: an average of 0.25R per trade.

25
00:02:20,726 --> 00:02:26,369
We ran 200 trades, 20,000 times, and counted how often the account was cut in half.

26
00:02:27,369 --> 00:02:31,809
At 1% and 2% risk: ruin was almost zero.

27
00:02:32,259 --> 00:02:35,969
At 5%: about 2% of the time.

28
00:02:36,418 --> 00:02:44,125
At 10%: about 18%. At 20%: 57% of the time.

29
00:02:44,575 --> 00:02:50,766
Same system, same edge. Only the size changed, and the outcome changed completely.

30
00:02:51,766 --> 00:02:55,083
There is also a simple formula, for a fixed lot size.

31
00:02:55,533 --> 00:03:03,971
When wins and losses are equal size, ruin chance is the loss probability divided by the win probability, to the power N.

32
00:03:04,421 --> 00:03:08,052
N means how many losses of room you have before ruin.

33
00:03:08,501 --> 00:03:17,671
At a 55% win rate, with room for five losses the ruin chance is 37%. With room for 25, it is under 1%.

34
00:03:18,671 --> 00:03:20,394
So how do you lower the risk of ruin?

35
00:03:20,845 --> 00:03:25,678
First: small risk per trade, one or two percent.

36
00:03:26,128 --> 00:03:31,769
Second: a daily or weekly loss limit. Hit it, and stop trading.

37
00:03:32,220 --> 00:03:39,926
Third: with no edge, no size is safe. A negative edge eats the account in the end.

38
00:03:40,926 --> 00:03:45,054
And most important: decide your ruin level in advance.

39
00:03:45,504 --> 00:03:51,146
For example: if the account falls 20%, I stop and re-check the whole system.

40
00:03:51,596 --> 00:03:55,802
Make this decision with a calm mind, not in the middle of a loss.

41
00:03:56,802 --> 00:03:58,291
So, today's summary.

42
00:03:58,741 --> 00:04:07,178
Ruin is a fall you can hardly recover from. Long losing streaks are very common.

43
00:04:07,628 --> 00:04:13,114
Even a good system can be sunk by big size. Keep risk at one or two percent.

44
00:04:13,564 --> 00:04:17,195
Use a loss limit, and set your ruin level in advance.

45
00:04:18,195 --> 00:04:23,681
